{#
contacts/_pane_actions.html.twig — the end of a contacts page's header: the
pane's window controls, ↗ full width (↙ back beside the mail when it is) and ×.
Rendered on the full page as well, which is the same pane
(contacts/_page_shell.html.twig), where the pair is ↙ and × .

The controls themselves are _partials/_pane_window_controls.html.twig, shared
with the calendar pane so the two have the same ends (#678). What is the
address book's own is the ↗'s href.

Included, so it reads `inPane` from contacts/_layout.html.twig.

The way out is the full-width position (contacts--pane#expand, #311): the
same pane given the row, the mail behind it, the contact as it is. The href
is for a middle click and a modified one, which are a new tab: the address
this page was asked for, so a contact open here is the one open there. A page
rendered WITH the mailbox has no address of its own (it is a sub-request) and
goes to the list.
#}
{% if inPane %}
    {% set pageUrl = true == app.request.attributes.get('_contacts_pane')
        ? path('app_contacts_list')
        : app.request.requestUri %}
    <span class="contents" data-contacts-pane-actions>
        {% include '_partials/_pane_window_controls.html.twig' with {
            controller:   'contacts--pane',
            expandUrl:    pageUrl,
            expandLabel:  'contacts.pane.mode.contacts'|trans,
            restoreLabel: 'contacts.pane.mode.split'|trans,
            closeLabel:   'contacts.pane.close'|trans,
        } only %}
    </span>
{% endif %}
